; APS6404L QSPI PSRAM data pump (DSPICOwithPSRAM hardware).
;
; Pin mapping:
; - OUT/IN base: GPIO22 (PSRAM IO0-IO3, 4 pins)
; - side-set   : GPIO26 (PSRAM SCLK)
; - CE (GPIO29) is handled by the CPU via SIO.
;
; This 5-word program runs on PIO1 SM2. The SDIO command program occupies
; instructions 14..31 and its RX/TX data programs dynamically share 5..13,
; leaving 0..4 for PSRAM. Moving the pump off PIO0 removes all runtime sharing
; with the timing-critical NDS cartridge SM0.
;
; CPU preloads X=7 and Y=number of quad nibbles minus one. IO0-IO3 are set as
; outputs/high before the SM starts. During the eight 1-bit OUTs only IO0
; changes, so IO1-IO3 remain high; the remaining OUTs drive all four pins.
; The TX FIFO stream
; starts with one packed word: serial command byte in bits 31:24 and the 24-bit
; address in bits 23:0. Subsequent words contain write data or read dummy bits.
; IRQ2 is a WAIT completion barrier: it leaves SCLK low and prevents
; wraparound from emitting an extra edge before the CPU disables the SM.
.program psram_qspi_command_tx
.side_set 1 opt
.wrap_target
serial_loop:
    out pins, 1         side 0
    jmp x-- serial_loop side 1
quad_loop:
    out pins, 4         side 0
    jmp y-- quad_loop   side 1
    irq wait 2          side 0  ; exact completion + park until CPU clears
.wrap
